# Pong (game-developer)

Browser Pong: you (left paddle) against the computer (right paddle); first to 5 points wins.

## Start it

- Open `index.html` in a desktop browser (double-click works), or serve the delivery
  directory with any static server, e.g. `python3 -m http.server 8000` and open
  <http://localhost:8000/>. No install or build step.
- `assets/` (sounds, logo, favicon) comes from the artist's repository; the game also
  runs without it, drawing everything itself and playing no sound.

## Controls

- W / S or Arrow Up / Down: move your paddle
- Enter or Space (or click): start, and play again from the end screen
- P or Esc: pause / resume; Q while paused: back to the title
- Esc on the end screen: back to the title (the end screen ignores input for its first second); M: sound on/off

## For checks

- `window.pong.getState()` (alias `pong.state()`) returns screen (`loading|title|play|over`),
  score, winner, ball, paddles, rallies and the asset load report; `pong.constants` gives sizes and speeds.
- `?seed=N` makes serve angles and the computer's aim errors reproducible.
- `node checks/sim.js attentive|casual|idle MATCHES [SEED] [LATENCY_MS]` runs src/game.js in Node with simulated
  time and a keyboard bot (intercept-predicting or ball-chasing) to measure difficulty in seconds.
- `checks/run_check.py GAME_DIR OUT_DIR` plays a full run in headless Chromium (Playwright):
  title, controls, a match the computer wins, play again, a match an anticipating keyboard bot
  wins, pause, and fails on any page error. Captures from runs are under `checks/`.

Asset contract with the artist: `docs/assets.md`.
